WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.213
Finally, governance, code and evidence.

2
00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:08.311
Governance means access is requested
through packages with approval and an expiry

3
00:00:08.311 --> 00:00:10.569
date, reviews run on a tiered schedule,

4
00:00:10.569 --> 00:00:13.337
and guests have sponsors
and get reviewed too.

5
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:15.406
As code means Conditional Access,

6
00:00:15.406 --> 00:00:18.950
PIM settings and access packages
live in version control.

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.717
Changes go through review
instead of the portal,

8
00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:24.000
and drift is watched against a baseline.

9
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.974
Evidence means all of this maps to the
federal access-control and monitoring

10
00:00:28.974 --> 00:00:34.025
controls, with every elevation and every
review on record; the slide lists them.

11
00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:36.063
And there are two traps in the tooling.

12
00:00:36.063 --> 00:00:40.466
Reviewing an application doesn't remove
members of the groups assigned to it,

13
00:00:40.466 --> 00:00:42.462
so the groups need their own review.

14
00:00:42.462 --> 00:00:46.257
And Entra keeps sign-in and
audit logs for only thirty days,

15
00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:49.320
so the evidence has to be
exported from day one.
